Logout: DELETE /api/session → on success navigate to default (manufacturer); on failure show error message "Error while trying to log you out." — that's what GWT does (HeaderMessages.errorLoggingOut). Given the API returns 500 on logout without login... The GWT app would show the error message. Faithful. But since the user was never logged in in our app, let me just attempt the call and handle both. Actually — GWT onLogoutSuccess → revealDefaultPlace → manufacturer. I'll do: call logout; regardless of outcome navigate to '/manufacturer'; on error also show error message. Simple.

