The not-migrated component has a title that's never set — let me instead set the title from route data. Actually simpler: remove the title input and hardcode? Or use route data:

```ts
{ path: 'cars', component: NotMigratedComponent, data: { title: 'Cars' } },
```

and in the component inject ActivatedRoute... That needs ActivatedRoute import. Quick approach: hardcode via separate instances? A component can't take params without route data. Let me use route data + ActivatedRoute snapshot:

```ts
export class NotMigratedComponent {
  private readonly route = inject(ActivatedRoute);
  title = this.route.snapshot.data['title'] ?? 'CarStore';
}
```

Hmm — `data['title']` with noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature=false → index access OK. Field initializer using inject() — inject works in field initializers ✓. But ActivatedRoute snapshot in constructor — data available at creation ✓.

Let me update that file quickly. Actually simpler and robust: just render a generic title without data. But nicer with the right title. I'll do the ActivatedRoute data approach.

